From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:08:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: the game description gives the culture victory as
 30000 points and a quarter more

Issue 243: patch 0043 set victory_min_points 30000 and a lead of a
quarter, but the description players read still said 8000 points and
half again as much.
---
 data/civ45/game.ruleset | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/game.ruleset b/data/civ45/game.ruleset
index 77b3a80..e54d659 100644
--- a/data/civ45/game.ruleset
+++ b/data/civ45/game.ruleset
@@ -47,8 +47,8 @@ can bombard a stack of two or more units, wounding every unit in it \
 and killing none. The map is a square grid seen from above that wraps \
 east to west, and each city works 21 tiles. \
 Six ways to win: conquest; domination (hold 60 percent of the land \
-and half the world's people for three turns); culture (8000 points \
-and half again as much as the runner-up); a spaceship that arrives; \
+and half the world's people for three turns); culture (30000 points \
+and a quarter more than the runner-up); a spaceship that arrives; \
 the last alliance standing; or the highest score when the game ends \
 after turn 475. \
 Also: strategic resources (Legion needs Iron, Armor needs Oil) and a \
